12827	RISK-110	A1006_Gipiškis2024	Preventing or mitigating data contamination and leakage	Data Governance	Developers of GPAIS and creators of benchmarks can take actions to prevent AI models from being trained on contaminated or leaked data, or mitigate such data contamination and leakage.For example, developers of AI models can try to find and remove contaminated or leaked data from the training corpus, and creators of benchmarks can help them by adding globally unique “canary strings” to the documents containing their benchmarks, which makes them easier to find [197]. More involved inter- ventions by benchmark-creators include restricting access to benchmarks over an API, or continually updating benchmarks to focus on recent data.
